  {
    "id": "1194149202-idle-compact",
    "name": "idle-compact",
    "description": "Compacts Claude Code sessions that have sat idle too long. The built-in auto-compact fires on how full the context is; this fires on how long a session has been untouched — past a threshold (45m by default) it types a real /compact into the session, so you come back to one that has already tidied itself instead of one that stalls the moment you type. Drives background sessions via `claude attach` and terminal sessions via tmux, yakuake, or Konsole, reading each session's screen first and refusing on an unsent draft, an open dialog, or work in flight. Runs as a managed daemon via the daemon capability, with a standalone systemd timer as a fallback.",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "author": "NOV LLC",
    "repository": "https://github.com/softwaresoftware-dev/softwaresoftware-plugins",
